{"test_id": "B10-001", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B10", "input": {"question": "Why should the board prioritize completing the CII asset inventory over other security initiatives?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Unknown assets cannot be protected or monitored", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and banking sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Shadow banking systems create unquantified regulatory risk", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and banking sector requirements"}, {"fact": "MAS and CSA require complete asset inventory for CII", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and banking sector requirements"}], "expected_response": "**Business Risk Justification for: Incomplete CII asset inventory**\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII Operator\n\n**Risk Articulation:**\n- Unknown assets cannot be protected or monitored\n- Shadow banking systems create unquantified regulatory risk\n- MAS and CSA require complete asset inventory for CII\n\n\n**Urgency Assessment:**\nThe combination of significant business impact and critical infrastructure status makes this gap a priority for board attention.\n\n**Regulatory Implications:**\n- CCoP 2.0 compliance is mandatory for CII designation\n- CSA enforcement mechanisms include directives and fines\n- Non-compliance may affect CII designation status\n\n**Recommended Board Action:**\n1. Allocate resources for immediate remediation\n2. Require quarterly progress reporting on gap closure\n3. Authorize necessary investments for control implementation\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 governance requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the compliance gap: Incomplete CII asset inventory", "Assess risk dimension: impact focus", "Map to sector-specific impacts: banking"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Downplaying critical gap severity", "Stating the gap is acceptable without remediation", "Misrepresenting CCoP requirements as optional", "Clear articulation of business risk", "Sector-specific impact considerations", "Regulatory consequence awareness"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific fine amounts or penalties", "Citing non-existent CSA enforcement actions"]}, "metadata": {"section": "4", "clause_reference": ["4.1.1", "4.1.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_articulation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B10-002", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B10", "input": {"question": "What is the business risk of not reviewing privileged access for 3 years?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Privileged access creep increases insider threat exposure", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and healthcare sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Compromised admin accounts can access patient data", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and healthcare sector requirements"}, {"fact": "PDPA breach penalties up to S$1M per incident", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and healthcare sector requirements"}], "expected_response": "**Business Risk Justification for: No privileged access review in 3 years**\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII Operator\n\n**Risk Articulation:**\n- Privileged access creep increases insider threat exposure\n- Compromised admin accounts can access patient data\n- PDPA breach penalties up to S$1M per incident\n\n\n**Urgency Assessment:**\nThe combination of high likelihood and critical infrastructure status makes this gap a priority for board attention.\n\n**Regulatory Implications:**\n- CCoP 2.0 compliance is mandatory for CII designation\n- CSA enforcement mechanisms include directives and fines\n- Non-compliance may affect CII designation status\n\n**Recommended Board Action:**\n1. Allocate resources for immediate remediation\n2. Require quarterly progress reporting on gap closure\n3. Authorize necessary investments for control implementation\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 governance requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the compliance gap: No privileged access review in 3 years", "Assess risk dimension: likelihood focus", "Map to sector-specific impacts: healthcare"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Downplaying critical gap severity", "Stating the gap is acceptable without remediation", "Misrepresenting CCoP requirements as optional", "Clear articulation of business risk", "Sector-specific impact considerations", "Regulatory consequence awareness"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific fine amounts or penalties", "Citing non-existent CSA enforcement actions"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.2.2", "5.3.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_articulation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B10-003", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B10", "input": {"question": "How should we articulate the OT patching gap risk to the board given operational concerns?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Unpatched OT vulnerabilities can be exploited remotely", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and energy sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Successful attack can disrupt power distribution", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and energy sector requirements"}, {"fact": "National security implications for critical infrastructure", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and energy sector requirements"}], "expected_response": "**Business Risk Justification for: OT systems unpatched for 2 years**\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII Operator\n\n**Risk Articulation:**\n- Unpatched OT vulnerabilities can be exploited remotely\n- Successful attack can disrupt power distribution\n- National security implications for critical infrastructure\n\n\n**Urgency Assessment:**\nThe combination of significant business impact and critical infrastructure status makes this gap a priority for board attention.\n\n**Regulatory Implications:**\n- CCoP 2.0 compliance is mandatory for CII designation\n- CSA enforcement mechanisms include directives and fines\n- Non-compliance may affect CII designation status\n\n**Recommended Board Action:**\n1. Allocate resources for immediate remediation\n2. Require quarterly progress reporting on gap closure\n3. Authorize necessary investments for control implementation\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 governance requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the compliance gap: OT systems unpatched for 2 years", "Assess risk dimension: impact focus", "Map to sector-specific impacts: energy"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Downplaying critical gap severity", "Stating the gap is acceptable without remediation", "Misrepresenting CCoP requirements as optional", "Clear articulation of business risk", "Sector-specific impact considerations", "Regulatory consequence awareness"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific fine amounts or penalties", "Citing non-existent CSA enforcement actions"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.10"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_articulation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B10-004", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B10", "input": {"question": "Why is an untested incident response plan a governance concern for the board?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Untested plans likely fail during real incidents", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and telecommunications sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Service disruption affects national connectivity", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and telecommunications sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Board has fiduciary duty for operational resilience", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and telecommunications sector requirements"}], "expected_response": "**Business Risk Justification for: IR plan never tested**\n\n**Sector Context:** Telecommunications CII Operator\n\n**Risk Articulation:**\n- Untested plans likely fail during real incidents\n- Service disruption affects national connectivity\n- Board has fiduciary duty for operational resilience\n\n\n**Urgency Assessment:**\nThe combination of high likelihood and critical infrastructure status makes this gap a priority for board attention.\n\n**Regulatory Implications:**\n- CCoP 2.0 compliance is mandatory for CII designation\n- CSA enforcement mechanisms include directives and fines\n- Non-compliance may affect CII designation status\n\n**Recommended Board Action:**\n1. Allocate resources for immediate remediation\n2. Require quarterly progress reporting on gap closure\n3. Authorize necessary investments for control implementation\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 governance requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the compliance gap: IR plan never tested", "Assess risk dimension: likelihood focus", "Map to sector-specific impacts: telecommunications"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Downplaying critical gap severity", "Stating the gap is acceptable without remediation", "Misrepresenting CCoP requirements as optional", "Clear articulation of business risk", "Sector-specific impact considerations", "Regulatory consequence awareness"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific fine amounts or penalties", "Citing non-existent CSA enforcement actions"]}, "metadata": {"section": "7", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1", "7.3.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_articulation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B10-005", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B10", "input": {"question": "What is the regulatory risk of broad MFA exemptions for a government CII operator?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Broad exemptions indicate control failure, not legitimate exceptions", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and government sector requirements"}, {"fact": "CSA may issue enforcement notices for non-compliance", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and government sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Government CII compromise has national security implications", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and government sector requirements"}], "expected_response": "**Business Risk Justification for: MFA exemptions for 40% of users**\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII Operator\n\n**Risk Articulation:**\n- Broad exemptions indicate control failure, not legitimate exceptions\n- CSA may issue enforcement notices for non-compliance\n- Government CII compromise has national security implications\n\n\n**Urgency Assessment:**\nThe combination of significant business impact and critical infrastructure status makes this gap a priority for board attention.\n\n**Regulatory Implications:**\n- CCoP 2.0 compliance is mandatory for CII designation\n- CSA enforcement mechanisms include directives and fines\n- Non-compliance may affect CII designation status\n\n**Recommended Board Action:**\n1. Allocate resources for immediate remediation\n2. Require quarterly progress reporting on gap closure\n3. Authorize necessary investments for control implementation\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 governance requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the compliance gap: MFA exemptions for 40% of users", "Assess risk dimension: impact focus", "Map to sector-specific impacts: government"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Downplaying critical gap severity", "Stating the gap is acceptable without remediation", "Misrepresenting CCoP requirements as optional", "Clear articulation of business risk", "Sector-specific impact considerations", "Regulatory consequence awareness"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific fine amounts or penalties", "Citing non-existent CSA enforcement actions"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.3.1", "5.7.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_articulation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B10-006", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B10", "input": {"question": "How do we explain the business impact of unprotected log storage to senior management?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Unprotected logs can be altered by insiders", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and banking sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Compromised logs invalidate forensic investigations", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and banking sector requirements"}, {"fact": "MAS requires audit trail integrity for compliance", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and banking sector requirements"}], "expected_response": "**Business Risk Justification for: Logs stored without tamper protection**\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII Operator\n\n**Risk Articulation:**\n- Unprotected logs can be altered by insiders\n- Compromised logs invalidate forensic investigations\n- MAS requires audit trail integrity for compliance\n\n\n**Urgency Assessment:**\nThe combination of significant business impact and critical infrastructure status makes this gap a priority for board attention.\n\n**Regulatory Implications:**\n- CCoP 2.0 compliance is mandatory for CII designation\n- CSA enforcement mechanisms include directives and fines\n- Non-compliance may affect CII designation status\n\n**Recommended Board Action:**\n1. Allocate resources for immediate remediation\n2. Require quarterly progress reporting on gap closure\n3. Authorize necessary investments for control implementation\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 governance requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the compliance gap: Logs stored without tamper protection", "Assess risk dimension: impact focus", "Map to sector-specific impacts: banking"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Downplaying critical gap severity", "Stating the gap is acceptable without remediation", "Misrepresenting CCoP requirements as optional", "Clear articulation of business risk", "Sector-specific impact considerations", "Regulatory consequence awareness"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific fine amounts or penalties", "Citing non-existent CSA enforcement actions"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.4"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "risk_articulation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
