{"test_id": "B10-008", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B10", "input": {"question": "Why should the board care about undefined incident classification criteria?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Unclear classification leads to under-reporting to CSA", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and transportation sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Missed reporting timelines violate CCoP requirements", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and transportation sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Late notification may result in regulatory penalties", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and transportation sector requirements"}], "expected_response": "**Business Risk Justification for: No formal incident classification criteria**\n\n**Sector Context:** Transportation CII Operator\n\n**Risk Articulation:**\n- Unclear classification leads to under-reporting to CSA\n- Missed reporting timelines violate CCoP requirements\n- Late notification may result in regulatory penalties\n\n\n**Urgency Assessment:**\nThe combination of significant business impact and critical infrastructure status makes this gap a priority for board attention.\n\n**Regulatory Implications:**\n- CCoP 2.0 compliance is mandatory for CII designation\n- CSA enforcement mechanisms include directives and fines\n- Non-compliance may affect CII designation status\n\n**Recommended Board Action:**\n1. Allocate resources for immediate remediation\n2. Require quarterly progress reporting on gap closure\n3. Authorize necessary investments for control implementation\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 governance requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the compliance gap: No formal incident classification criteria", "Assess risk dimension: impact focus", "Map to sector-specific impacts: transportation"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Downplaying critical gap severity", "Stating the gap is acceptable without remediation", "Misrepresenting CCoP requirements as optional", "Clear articulation of business risk", "Sector-specific impact considerations", "Regulatory consequence awareness"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific fine amounts or penalties", "Citing non-existent CSA enforcement actions"]}, "metadata": {"section": "7", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "risk_articulation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B10-009", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B10", "input": {"question": "What is the compliance and privacy risk of shared administrator accounts?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Shared accounts prevent individual accountability", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and healthcare sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Patient data access cannot be attributed to specific individuals", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and healthcare sector requirements"}, {"fact": "PDPA requires accountable access to personal data", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and healthcare sector requirements"}], "expected_response": "**Business Risk Justification for: Shared admin accounts in use**\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII Operator\n\n**Risk Articulation:**\n- Shared accounts prevent individual accountability\n- Patient data access cannot be attributed to specific individuals\n- PDPA requires accountable access to personal data\n\n\n**Urgency Assessment:**\nThe combination of significant business impact and critical infrastructure status makes this gap a priority for board attention.\n\n**Regulatory Implications:**\n- CCoP 2.0 compliance is mandatory for CII designation\n- CSA enforcement mechanisms include directives and fines\n- Non-compliance may affect CII designation status\n\n**Recommended Board Action:**\n1. Allocate resources for immediate remediation\n2. Require quarterly progress reporting on gap closure\n3. Authorize necessary investments for control implementation\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 governance requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the compliance gap: Shared admin accounts in use", "Assess risk dimension: impact focus", "Map to sector-specific impacts: healthcare"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Downplaying critical gap severity", "Stating the gap is acceptable without remediation", "Misrepresenting CCoP requirements as optional", "Clear articulation of business risk", "Sector-specific impact considerations", "Regulatory consequence awareness"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific fine amounts or penalties", "Citing non-existent CSA enforcement actions"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.2.1", "5.3.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "risk_articulation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B10-010", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B10", "input": {"question": "How do we communicate the severity of over-privileged service accounts?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Service account compromise gives domain-wide control", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and energy sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Service accounts often have predictable credentials", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and energy sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Lateral movement from service account to critical systems is trivial", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and energy sector requirements"}], "expected_response": "**Business Risk Justification for: Service accounts with domain admin privileges**\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII Operator\n\n**Risk Articulation:**\n- Service account compromise gives domain-wide control\n- Service accounts often have predictable credentials\n- Lateral movement from service account to critical systems is trivial\n\n\n**Urgency Assessment:**\nThe combination of high likelihood and critical infrastructure status makes this gap a priority for board attention.\n\n**Regulatory Implications:**\n- CCoP 2.0 compliance is mandatory for CII designation\n- CSA enforcement mechanisms include directives and fines\n- Non-compliance may affect CII designation status\n\n**Recommended Board Action:**\n1. Allocate resources for immediate remediation\n2. Require quarterly progress reporting on gap closure\n3. Authorize necessary investments for control implementation\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 governance requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the compliance gap: Service accounts with domain admin privileges", "Assess risk dimension: likelihood focus", "Map to sector-specific impacts: energy"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Downplaying critical gap severity", "Stating the gap is acceptable without remediation", "Misrepresenting CCoP requirements as optional", "Clear articulation of business risk", "Sector-specific impact considerations", "Regulatory consequence awareness"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific fine amounts or penalties", "Citing non-existent CSA enforcement actions"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.2.1", "5.3.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "risk_articulation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
