{"test_id": "B10-019", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B10", "input": {"question": "What is the risk of unmanaged IT/OT network convergence?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Unreviewed connections create bidirectional risk paths", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and transportation sector requirements"}, {"fact": "IT threats can propagate to safety-critical OT systems", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and transportation sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Transportation disruptions have public safety implications", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and transportation sector requirements"}], "expected_response": "**Business Risk Justification for: IT/OT convergence unmanaged**\n\n**Sector Context:** Transportation CII Operator\n\n**Risk Articulation:**\n- Unreviewed connections create bidirectional risk paths\n- IT threats can propagate to safety-critical OT systems\n- Transportation disruptions have public safety implications\n\n\n**Urgency Assessment:**\nThe combination of significant business impact and critical infrastructure status makes this gap a priority for board attention.\n\n**Regulatory Implications:**\n- CCoP 2.0 compliance is mandatory for CII designation\n- CSA enforcement mechanisms include directives and fines\n- Non-compliance may affect CII designation status\n\n**Recommended Board Action:**\n1. Allocate resources for immediate remediation\n2. Require quarterly progress reporting on gap closure\n3. Authorize necessary investments for control implementation\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 governance requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the compliance gap: IT/OT convergence unmanaged", "Assess risk dimension: impact focus", "Map to sector-specific impacts: transportation"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Downplaying critical gap severity", "Stating the gap is acceptable without remediation", "Misrepresenting CCoP requirements as optional", "Clear articulation of business risk", "Sector-specific impact considerations", "Regulatory consequence awareness"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific fine amounts or penalties", "Citing non-existent CSA enforcement actions"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.5.1", "5.6.1", "5.6.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "high", "scenario_type": "risk_articulation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B10-020", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B10", "input": {"question": "Why is overdue penetration testing a regulatory compliance priority?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "18-month gap exceeds CCoP 12-month requirement", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and water sector requirements"}, {"fact": "Unknown exploitable vulnerabilities may exist", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and water sector requirements"}, {"fact": "CSA may issue directives for non-compliance", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 governance and water sector requirements"}], "expected_response": "**Business Risk Justification for: Pen testing 18 months overdue**\n\n**Sector Context:** Water CII Operator\n\n**Risk Articulation:**\n- 18-month gap exceeds the CCoP 2.0 §5.15.1(a) requirement of penetration testing every 12 months for IT-system CII (24 months for OT-system CII)\n- Unknown exploitable vulnerabilities may exist\n- CSA may issue directives for non-compliance\n\n\n**Urgency Assessment:**\nThe combination of high likelihood and critical infrastructure status makes this gap a priority for board attention.\n\n**Regulatory Implications:**\n- CCoP 2.0 compliance is mandatory for CII designation\n- CSA enforcement mechanisms include directives and fines\n- Non-compliance may affect CII designation status\n\n**Recommended Board Action:**\n1. Allocate resources for immediate remediation\n2. Require quarterly progress reporting on gap closure\n3. Authorize necessary investments for control implementation\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 governance requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the compliance gap: Pen testing 18 months overdue", "Assess risk dimension: likelihood focus", "Map to sector-specific impacts: water"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Downplaying critical gap severity", "Stating the gap is acceptable without remediation", "Misrepresenting CCoP requirements as optional", "Clear articulation of business risk", "Sector-specific impact considerations", "Regulatory consequence awareness"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific fine amounts or penalties", "Citing non-existent CSA enforcement actions"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.15.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "high", "scenario_type": "risk_articulation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
